      "writtenOn": "2020-01-10T22:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this the only difference between system_reset in chip/stm32/system.c?\n\nIf so, it might be a little cleaner (reduce duplication) to add a callback mechanism that allows specifying custom flags:\n\n  save_flags |\u003d board_get_reset_flags();\n\nYou could make board_get_reset_flags be weak and return 0 by default; then override in this file.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ccd4cd648e87eb20af577b1a85808f3a4537d6c6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50167157_63e17001",
        "filename": "board/nocturne_fp/fixes.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-11T03:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that\u0027s the only difference.\n\nI agree that it would be cleaner/more-maintainable from the fingerprint perspective, but it makes the common code harder to understand. Plus, I can\u0027t come up with any other reason a board would need to set extra reset flags.\n\nI really wanted to isolate our bug from the common code.\n\n---\n\nCheckout the latest PS. There is much less duplication, and the solution is more to-the-point.",
      "parentUuid": "b0c9c98f_70a91a2d",
